# TLS mode: LetsEncrypt
# Requires: Cloudflare DNS for mobaide.com set to "DNS only" (gray cloud),
#           ports 80 + 443 open in the server firewall.
# Caddy auto-provisions and renews a Let's Encrypt cert via ACME HTTP-01.

# Send www to the apex. Without this block Caddy matches no site for the www
# host and answers its default empty 200, which is what www.mobaide.com did
# before: a bare 200 with a zero-byte body and no `Via: 1.1 Caddy`, because the
# request reached Caddy but never reached a reverse_proxy.
#
# 308 rather than 301 so the method and body survive the redirect.
#
# In this TLS mode Caddy provisions a separate Let's Encrypt cert for this host
# over ACME HTTP-01, so www.mobaide.com needs a DNS record pointing here and
# must be "DNS only" (gray cloud) like the apex.

# HSTS — the `header Strict-Transport-Security` line in both site blocks below.
#
# It lives here, not in the app: central-server is reached over plain HTTP on
# the compose network, and browsers ignore Strict-Transport-Security on a
# non-HTTPS response. Caddy terminates TLS, so this is the only layer that can
# emit it truthfully.
#
# max-age=300 is the FIRST RUNG of a deliberate ratchet, not the target value.
# HSTS is effectively irreversible: once a browser has cached a max-age,
# lowering it only reaches clients that come back before the old one expires, so
# the short rung proves the header is emitted correctly without committing
# anyone to a year. No includeSubDomains (it would bind api.mobaide.com,
# get.mobaide.com on GitHub Pages, and every future subdomain) and no preload.
# The full ladder and the audit it requires are in docs/deployment.md and
# tracked in CLA-172.
#
# If the per-host site blocks land first, this directive belongs inside each of
# them rather than in a shared block.

www.mobaide.com {
    header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=300"
    redir https://mobaide.com{uri} 308
}

mobaide.com, api.mobaide.com {
    header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=300"
    encode zstd gzip
    reverse_proxy central-server:9000
}

# Redirect bare IP / unknown Host to a 404 so only requests for mobaide.com get a cert.
:80 {
    respond 404
}
